  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Stonex Financial obligated $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Stonex Financial won 341 awards so far in the fiscal year, and the average award size is $3.5M. Stonex Financial obligations are down 10.4% year over year. Historical obligations show a rise and fall pattern: FY21 obligatons were $1.1B, FY22 obligatons were $1.7B, FY23 obligatons were $1.7B, FY24 obligatons were $703M, FY25 obligatons were $1.3B, and FY26 obligatons are $1.2B. The current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and the reported figures are contract obligations except for award-value items in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Use these figures to assess scale and recent direction: Stonex Financial remains a multi-hundred-million-dollar federal vendor in FY2026 to date, with fewer obligations than the prior full year on a year-over-year basis.",
